addclaim(112,921,6,[81],'18–23','Paraphrase: abelian categories with exact functors are listed, followed by the question additive functors?','Additive functors between abelian categories need not be exact. Exactness is additional doctrine data, so the two entries cannot be interchanged.','open parenthetical question','Tensoring abelian groups with Z/2 is additive but sends the monomorphism2:Z→Z to the zero endomorphism of Z/2, which is not monic. Thus it is not left exact. Additivity only preserves the finite biproduct structure, not all kernels and cokernels.','Stacks00HK states the exact relation between tensor exactness and flatness. The explicit multiplication-by2 witness answers the parenthetical question.',['StacksFlatness'])
addclaim(113,926,7,[112],'714–726','Paraphrase: replace the relative classifier by a stack of structures and a stack of slice topoi; the sentence stops.','For a fixed small finite-limit theory and fixed base objects in X, assigning to U the category of structures on their pullbacks in X/U is a stack for the canonical topology, by descent of objects, arrows, equations and finite-limit cones. The fragment does not specify a complete equivalence between this stack and its proposed stack of slice topoi.','construction sketched and left unfinished','Descent is effective in a topos. A finite-limit model is a family of objects/arrows satisfying equations and invertibility of comparison maps; these properties descend along epimorphic covers, as do the chosen underlying-object isomorphisms. This proves the stated model stack. Identifying the unfinished topos-valued object or using it to replace the relative classifier requires the missing variance and2-morphism conventions.','Vistoli’s descent framework, Stacks04WA and Vickers5.11–5.12 supply the established model-stack and relative-classifier ingredients. The last incomplete sentence is not promoted to a fully specified topos-stack theorem.',['VistoliDescent','StacksPullback','Vickers2017'],'C')

addproblem(60,'Faithful bases versus operation generation',[occurrence(7,[102],'309–315')],'Does a basis detecting transformations generate all objects by lambda operations?','No for empty operations or finite products; the finite-limit variant requires a separately stated hypothesis.','C101 gives the Karoubi and even-cardinality witnesses, matched to Kelly5.36 and ALR2003.',['Kelly1982','AdamekLawvereRosicky2003'],worth='Commentary work for the stated converse; a further task is worthwhile only for a precisely strengthened finite-limit or retract-closed version.')
addproblem(61,'Intrinsic recovery of the construction category',[occurrence(7,[107],'555–595')],'Can Sigma be characterized from S=T(Set) alone?','Finite-limit theories are recovered by S_fp; finite-product presentations only up to Morita/Cauchy data. The proposed arbitrary-lambda criterion is not yet intrinsic.','C104 identifies the circular quantification and the exact established special cases.',['LackPower2009','AdamekLawvereRosicky2003','Kelly1982'],worth='Worth a focused comparison of two specific doctrines; first remove the explicit occurrences of T from the candidate definition of Sigma.')
addproblem(62,'The corrected Yoneda comparison',[occurrence(7,[109],'597–644','bijection deleted at614; proved for representables at622')],'Is the displayed application a bijection for every X?','Only the representable case is proved, and the general claim is false.','C105 gives the complete Yoneda proof and the C=1,U=1,X=empty counterexample.',['RiehlContextOnline'],worth='Commentary work only: preserve the manuscript’s own correction and include the0-versus1 test.')
addproblem(63,'Inverse image of a stack through Pro(C)',[occurrence(7,[110],'645–684')],'How does extension to Pro(C) compute inverse image, including a subsite?','Use the opposite of the cofiltered comma category, a2-colimit, and stackification for the indicated topology.','C106 matches Stacks8.12.5–8.12.10; the ordinary-colimit and variance shortcuts are excluded.',['StacksPullback','VistoliDescent'],worth='Worth a bounded explanatory reconstruction: work one nontrivial groupoid-valued stack through the comma formula and its descent step.')
addproblem(64,'Relative classifier with fixed underlying objects',[occurrence(7,[112],'687–712')],'Does the2-fiber product B×_(B_I)X exist and classify the specified structures?','Yes for Grothendieck topoi, with chosen isomorphisms of underlying objects.','C107 proves the exact universal property and matches SGAIV9.1.6(d) and Vickers5.11–5.12.',['SGA4I1972','Vickers2017'],worth='A commentary and one explicit worked example are worthwhile; the existence theorem and relative universal property are established.')
addproblem(65,'The unfinished stack of structures and slice topoi',[occurrence(7,[112],'714–726')],'How is the stack of structures related to the sketched stack of topoi?','The category-valued structure stack exists by descent; the topos-valued comparison requires the missing conventions and definition.','C113 proves the precise first construction and delimits the final unfinished assertion.',['VistoliDescent','StacksPullback','Vickers2017'],worth='Worth a separate bounded task after the ink clarifies the final symbols; begin with the category-valued model stack and its relation to the relative classifier.')
addproblem(66,'Comparison with Lazard’s analyseurs',[occurrence(6,[90],'339')],'What is the relation with Lazard’s analyseurs?','Compare finite-arity substitution first, then account separately for multigrading and formal completion.','C108 uses the actual definitions in Lazard Bourbaki109§§4–6 and does not infer equivalence from the shared algebraic vocabulary.',['Lazard1956'],worth='Worth a historically focused translation task, starting with one explicit polynomial analyser and its finite-product theory.')
addproblem(67,'Finiteness properties in the ring lattice',[occurrence(3,[37],'48–53;90–92;123–133')],'Which listed finiteness and singularity properties are geometric?','The usual noetherian and finite-presentation versions fail filtered-colimit closure; alternative nonnoetherian meanings require definition.','C109 gives polynomial and Boolean-ring directed systems checking all the stated negative annotations.',['SGA4I1972','StacksFlatness'],worth='Commentary work for the usual meanings; inspect the ambiguous regularity abbreviation before considering a different nonnoetherian notion.')
addproblem(68,'Nondegenerate classifier without Set models',[occurrence(2,[24],'168–174')],'Can the Set-valued model category be empty without the classifier being degenerate?','Yes, for a complete atomless Boolean locale.','C110 matches Barr1974p265 and gives the full atom obstruction.',['Barr1974'],worth='Commentary work only: the exact classical counterexample prevents an erroneous enough-points inference.')
addproblem(69,'Detached cohomology and ring-topology fragments',[occurrence(2,[34],'540–544','coefficient and arrow unclear'),occurrence(3,[38],'206–244','upside-down expressions; nested P1,P2 query')],'The fragments contain a cohomology expression, an n-model limit and an unexplained nested pair P1,P2.','No precise strongest theorem is recoverable from these supplied transcriptions.','C111 records the unsuccessful identification searches and preserves all alternatives.',['SGA4I1972','Lazard1956'],worth='Scan-first only: further mathematical development would require inventing missing definitions, so the next task should inspect these exact fragments and their layout.')
addproblem(70,'Additive or exact functors between abelian categories',[occurrence(6,[81],'18–23')],'Can additive functors be used instead of exact ones in the abelian doctrine?','No; tensoring with Z/2 is additive but not left exact.','C112 gives the explicit kernel test, with the flatness criterion as the exact reference.',['StacksFlatness'],worth='Commentary work only: the distinction is settled by a single tensor calculation.')

